  %h3
    %a{ href: "https://files.eric.ed.gov/fulltext/EJ1378311.pdf", target: "_blank" }
      Design Specifications of Augmentative and Alternative Communication Apps for Individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder
  %cite
    Polat, H., & Delialioglu, O. (2023).
    %em International Journal of Technology in Education (IJTE)
    , 6(1), 19-36.
    %a{ href: "https://doi.org/10.46328/ijte.396", target: "_blank" } https://doi.org/10.46328/ijte.396
  %p
    This analysis informed the design choices behind Pick-a-Pic by emphasizing the importance of these qualities in AAC apps:
  %ul
    %li Just-in-time customization
    %li Ease of use and design
    %li Ease of customization of voice and %arrangement 
    %li TODO: INSERT OTHER RECOMMENDED FEATURES

  %h3
    %a{ href: "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9266194/", target: "_blank" }
      Parents' Perceptions and Experiences with Their Children's Use of Augmentative/Alternative Communication: A Systematic Review and Qualitative Meta-Synthesis
  %cite
    Berenguer, C.; Martínez, E.R.; De Stasio, S.; Baixauli, I.
    %em Int. J. Environ. Res. Public Health
    \ 2022, 19, 8091.
    %a{ href: "https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph19138091", target: "_blank" } https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph19138091
  %p
    This analysis validated our own experience with the barriers that prevented learners and caregivers from using their AAC apps:
    %ul
      %li High cost
      %li Time investment
      %li Training needed
      %li Lack of individualization
      %li Inconsistent use across settings

  %h3
    %a{ href: "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10882-021-09803-y", target: "_blank" }
      A Systematic Review of Research Comparing Mobile Technology Speech-Generating Devices to Other AAC Modes with Individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder
  %cite
    Lorah, E.R., Holyfield, C., Miller, J. et al.
    %em J Dev Phys Disabil
    \ 34, 187-210 (2022).
    %a{ href: "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10882-021-09803-y", target: "_blank" } https://doi.org/10.1007/s10882-021-09803-y
  %p
    This analysis validated the core assumption of our app &mdash; that individuals learning the basics of functional communication
    were not being served by complex AAC apps and instead needed something rooted in the simplicity of PECS.

  %h3
    %a{ href: "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40489-022-00334-6", target: "_blank" }
      A Systematic Review of Evidence-based Instruction for Individuals with Autism Using Mobile Augmentative and Alternative Communication Technology
  %cite
    Lorah, E.R., Holyfield, C., Griffen, B. et al.
    %em Rev J Autism Dev Disord
    \ 11, 210-224 (2024).
    %a{ href: "https://doi.org/10.1007/s40489-022-00334-6", target: "_blank" } https://doi.org/10.1007/s40489-022-00334-6
  %p This analysis validated the ways that we envision Pick-a-Pic being useful in educational settings.

